  GUARD MAP — where the spiral could have been broken:
    L0/L5 client+gateway  
      fail : stream held open forever by heartbeats
      guard: hard total-duration timeout on the client AND gateway
      armed: NO
    L4 scheduler          
      fail : max_tokens=null — no ceiling exists
      guard: always set max_tokens / deadline / wall-clock budget
      armed: NO
    L4 sampler            
      fail : rep_penalty=1.0, eos≈0 — circling is free
      guard: repetition penalty >1.0, n-gram blocklist, stop strings
      armed: OFF by default
    L4 decode loop        
      fail : no progress check between iterations
      guard: loop detector: logits entropy / n-gram repetition monitor
      armed: NO
    L2 KV cache           
      fail : monotonic growth, never compacted
      guard: summarization/compaction at context thresholds
      armed: rarely
    L8 hardware           
      fail : 97% util doing useless math — no waste signal
      guard: waste alarm: work done vs. output delivered
      armed: NO
    billing               
      fail : per-token meter runs perfectly during the spiral
      guard: budget cutoff that halts generation
      armed: available, often unset
    the human             
      fail : watches a spinner
      guard: Ctrl+C
      armed: YES — 4/4. the only control that worked.

  bottom line for security engineering:
    every automated layer was present and healthy. zero automated guards
    fired. the spiral lived in the gap between 'nothing failed' and
    'nobody stopped it.' instrument the meaning layers (L0–L6): timeouts,
    ceilings, loop detectors, budgets. below that: physics. physics is fine.

  the question outlasted HTTP, CUDA, silicon, atoms, nuclei, quarks,
  fields, and the planck wall. the loop was never in the machine.
  the machine was a place the loop briefly stopped.
